1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,190
Almost four hundred years ago,

2
00:00:02,190 --> 00:00:07,290
a scientist called Jan van Helmont
planted a small willow tree in a pot of

3
00:00:07,290 --> 00:00:08,520
dried soil.

4
00:00:08,520 --> 00:00:10,380
He weighed the tree.

5
00:00:10,380 --> 00:00:12,240
He weighed the soil.

6
00:00:12,240 --> 00:00:14,080
Then, for five years,

7
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:18,640
he gave it nothing but
water. The tree grew.

8
00:00:18,640 --> 00:00:22,910
It gained about seventy-four
kilograms. And the soil?

9
00:00:22,910 --> 00:00:26,140
It had lost only about
fifty-seven grams.

10
00:00:26,840 --> 00:00:32,800
So where did a whole tree's worth
of mass come from? Not the soil.

11
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:36,110
Most of the wood came
out of thin air.

12
00:00:36,510 --> 00:00:38,540
By the end of this video,

13
00:00:38,540 --> 00:00:40,290
you'll know exactly how,

14
00:00:40,290 --> 00:00:43,260
and how to explain it in an exam.

15
00:00:48,810 --> 00:00:52,380
You eat to get your
food. Plants don't.

16
00:00:52,380 --> 00:00:54,420
Plants make their own food,

17
00:00:54,420 --> 00:00:56,100
by photosynthesis.

18
00:00:56,500 --> 00:00:59,780
Here's the definition
the mark scheme wants.

19
00:00:59,780 --> 00:01:02,180
Learn it word for word.

20
00:01:02,180 --> 00:01:06,540
Photosynthesis is the process by
which plants synthesise carbohydrates

21
00:01:06,540 --> 00:01:09,920
from raw materials
using energy from light.

22
00:01:10,820 --> 00:01:12,730
Let's break that down.

23
00:01:12,730 --> 00:01:14,600
Synthesise means make.

24
00:01:14,600 --> 00:01:17,230
The carbohydrate it makes is glucose,

25
00:01:17,230 --> 00:01:18,750
a simple sugar.

26
00:01:18,750 --> 00:01:22,320
The raw materials are
carbon dioxide and water.

27
00:01:22,320 --> 00:01:25,780
And the energy to do
it comes from light.

28
00:01:26,730 --> 00:01:28,690
Now the word equation.

29
00:01:28,690 --> 00:01:30,830
Carbon dioxide, plus water,

30
00:01:30,830 --> 00:01:33,330
gives glucose, plus oxygen.

31
00:01:33,630 --> 00:01:37,570
And it happens in the presence
of light and chlorophyll,

32
00:01:37,570 --> 00:01:40,250
so we write those on the arrow.

33
00:01:40,250 --> 00:01:42,950
They're conditions, not reactants.

34
00:01:42,950 --> 00:01:44,700
Light isn't a substance,

35
00:01:44,700 --> 00:01:47,200
and chlorophyll isn't used up.

36
00:01:47,700 --> 00:01:50,920
So where do the raw
materials come from?

37
00:01:50,920 --> 00:01:54,780
Carbon dioxide diffuses
into the leaf from the air.

38
00:01:54,780 --> 00:01:58,080
Water is absorbed from
the soil by the roots,

39
00:01:58,080 --> 00:01:59,970
and travels up the stem,

40
00:01:59,970 --> 00:02:02,600
in the xylem, to the leaf.

41
00:02:02,900 --> 00:02:05,150
Oxygen is a waste product.

42
00:02:05,150 --> 00:02:08,260
Some is used in the
plant's own respiration,

43
00:02:08,260 --> 00:02:12,640
and the rest diffuses out
of the leaf, into the air.

44
00:02:13,590 --> 00:02:17,750
You also need to know the
balanced symbol equation.

45
00:02:17,750 --> 00:02:21,090
Six C O two, plus six H two O,

46
00:02:21,090 --> 00:02:23,760
gives C six H twelve O six,

47
00:02:23,760 --> 00:02:25,620
plus six O two.

48
00:02:26,120 --> 00:02:28,130
Let's check it balances.

49
00:02:28,130 --> 00:02:30,290
Carbon: six on the left,

50
00:02:30,290 --> 00:02:32,000
six on the right.

51
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:34,720
Hydrogen: twelve on each side.

52
00:02:34,720 --> 00:02:38,590
Oxygen: twelve plus six
makes eighteen on the left,

53
00:02:38,590 --> 00:02:43,680
and six plus twelve makes eighteen
on the right. It balances.

54
00:02:44,630 --> 00:02:47,850
So, what does the light actually do?

55
00:02:48,150 --> 00:02:51,570
Inside the cells of a
leaf are chloroplasts.

56
00:02:51,570 --> 00:02:53,730
Chloroplasts contain chlorophyll,

57
00:02:53,730 --> 00:02:55,600
a green pigment.

58
00:02:55,600 --> 00:02:57,670
Chlorophyll absorbs light.

59
00:02:57,670 --> 00:03:01,860
Then it transfers energy from
light into energy in chemicals,

60
00:03:01,860 --> 00:03:04,560
for the synthesis of carbohydrates.

61
00:03:04,560 --> 00:03:08,950
In other words, that energy
ends up stored in glucose.

62
00:03:09,450 --> 00:03:12,190
Be careful with your wording here.

63
00:03:12,190 --> 00:03:15,330
Never write that
chlorophyll makes energy.

64
00:03:15,330 --> 00:03:17,190
Energy can't be made.

65
00:03:17,190 --> 00:03:19,210
Chlorophyll transfers it.

66
00:03:19,210 --> 00:03:22,420
So use the syllabus word: transfers.

67
00:03:25,570 --> 00:03:28,110
So the plant has made glucose.

68
00:03:28,110 --> 00:03:29,920
What happens to it?

69
00:03:29,920 --> 00:03:32,510
There are five uses to learn.

70
00:03:32,810 --> 00:03:35,840
One. Glucose is used in respiration,

71
00:03:35,840 --> 00:03:38,920
to release energy for
the plant's cells.

72
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:41,900
Two. Glucose is turned into starch,

73
00:03:41,900 --> 00:03:43,710
as an energy store.

74
00:03:43,710 --> 00:03:45,220
Starch is insoluble,

75
00:03:45,220 --> 00:03:49,760
so storing it doesn't affect the
movement of water by osmosis.

76
00:03:49,760 --> 00:03:53,130
Three. Glucose is used
to make cellulose,

77
00:03:53,130 --> 00:03:55,480
which builds the cell walls.

78
00:03:55,480 --> 00:03:59,990
Four. Glucose is changed
into sucrose, another sugar.

79
00:03:59,990 --> 00:04:02,620
Sucrose is transported in the phloem,

80
00:04:02,620 --> 00:04:06,190
to other parts of
the plant. And five.

81
00:04:06,190 --> 00:04:08,520
Sugars are used to make nectar,

82
00:04:08,520 --> 00:04:12,290
in flowers, to attract
insects for pollination.

83
00:04:12,790 --> 00:04:14,920
Respiration. Starch.

84
00:04:14,920 --> 00:04:18,040
Cellulose. Sucrose. Nectar.

85
00:04:21,190 --> 00:04:23,530
But glucose only contains carbon,

86
00:04:23,530 --> 00:04:25,300
hydrogen and oxygen.

87
00:04:25,300 --> 00:04:28,210
To grow, a plant also needs proteins,

88
00:04:28,210 --> 00:04:31,290
and proteins are made
from amino acids.

89
00:04:31,290 --> 00:04:33,900
Amino acids contain nitrogen.

90
00:04:33,900 --> 00:04:37,060
So plants absorb nitrate
ions from the soil,

91
00:04:37,060 --> 00:04:38,830
through their roots.

92
00:04:38,830 --> 00:04:42,250
Nitrate ions are needed
to make amino acids.

93
00:04:42,250 --> 00:04:43,910
Without enough nitrate,

94
00:04:43,910 --> 00:04:46,050
the plant has stunted growth,

95
00:04:46,050 --> 00:04:48,840
and its older leaves turn yellow.

96
00:04:49,340 --> 00:04:51,990
Plants also absorb magnesium ions.

97
00:04:51,990 --> 00:04:55,420
Magnesium ions are needed
to make chlorophyll.

98
00:04:55,420 --> 00:04:57,180
Without enough magnesium,

99
00:04:57,180 --> 00:05:00,360
the leaves turn yellow
between the veins.

100
00:05:00,360 --> 00:05:03,530
Less chlorophyll means
less light is absorbed,

101
00:05:03,530 --> 00:05:05,990
so there's less photosynthesis.

102
00:05:06,490 --> 00:05:09,040
In an exam, link three things:

103
00:05:09,040 --> 00:05:11,650
the ion, what it's used to make,

104
00:05:11,650 --> 00:05:14,100
and what happens without it.

105
00:05:17,250 --> 00:05:20,130
Most photosynthesis
happens in the leaves,

106
00:05:20,130 --> 00:05:22,970
and leaves are adapted for it.

107
00:05:22,970 --> 00:05:25,560
Most leaves are broad and thin.

108
00:05:25,560 --> 00:05:27,990
Broad means a large surface area,

109
00:05:27,990 --> 00:05:29,900
to absorb more light.

110
00:05:29,900 --> 00:05:34,620
Thin means a short distance for carbon
dioxide to diffuse to the cells

111
00:05:34,620 --> 00:05:35,660
inside.

112
00:05:36,160 --> 00:05:38,450
Now let's cut a leaf open.

113
00:05:38,450 --> 00:05:43,240
This is a cross-section through
the leaf of a dicotyledonous plant.

114
00:05:43,240 --> 00:05:46,900
That's a plant whose seeds
have two seed leaves.

115
00:05:46,900 --> 00:05:49,310
It's a simplified diagram.

116
00:05:49,310 --> 00:05:52,600
For each part, you
need to know its name,

117
00:05:52,600 --> 00:05:55,150
and how it helps photosynthesis.

118
00:05:55,150 --> 00:05:59,240
Let's go through it layer
by layer, from the top.

119
00:05:59,740 --> 00:06:01,990
First, the waxy cuticle.

120
00:06:01,990 --> 00:06:03,690
It reduces water loss,

121
00:06:03,690 --> 00:06:05,690
and because it's transparent,

122
00:06:05,690 --> 00:06:08,590
light passes straight through it.

123
00:06:08,590 --> 00:06:10,940
Next, the upper epidermis.

124
00:06:10,940 --> 00:06:13,230
These cells are transparent too,

125
00:06:13,230 --> 00:06:15,420
and they have no chloroplasts,

126
00:06:15,420 --> 00:06:19,090
so light passes through
to the cells below.

127
00:06:19,090 --> 00:06:21,350
Then the palisade mesophyll.

128
00:06:21,350 --> 00:06:23,000
These cells are tall,

129
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:26,110
tightly packed, close
to the top surface,

130
00:06:26,110 --> 00:06:28,220
and full of chloroplasts.

131
00:06:28,220 --> 00:06:30,760
So they absorb the most light.

132
00:06:30,760 --> 00:06:34,000
This is where most
photosynthesis happens.

133
00:06:34,950 --> 00:06:38,230
Below the palisade is
the spongy mesophyll.

134
00:06:38,230 --> 00:06:39,930
Its cells are rounder,

135
00:06:39,930 --> 00:06:41,390
and loosely packed,

136
00:06:41,390 --> 00:06:43,790
with air spaces between them.

137
00:06:43,790 --> 00:06:47,680
The air spaces let carbon
dioxide diffuse to the cells,

138
00:06:47,680 --> 00:06:51,780
and they give a large surface
area for gas exchange.

139
00:06:52,280 --> 00:06:55,710
Running through the leaf
are vascular bundles.

140
00:06:55,710 --> 00:06:59,810
The xylem brings water and
mineral ions into the leaf.

141
00:06:59,810 --> 00:07:03,170
The phloem carries sucrose
and amino acids away,

142
00:07:03,170 --> 00:07:05,560
to the rest of the plant.

143
00:07:06,060 --> 00:07:08,930
On the underside is
the lower epidermis,

144
00:07:08,930 --> 00:07:11,430
with tiny pores called stomata.

145
00:07:11,430 --> 00:07:13,820
One pore is called a stoma.

146
00:07:13,820 --> 00:07:17,040
Carbon dioxide diffuses
in through the stomata,

147
00:07:17,040 --> 00:07:19,100
and oxygen diffuses out.

148
00:07:19,100 --> 00:07:23,530
Each stoma is opened and closed
by a pair of guard cells.

149
00:07:23,530 --> 00:07:26,390
In the light, they open the stomata,

150
00:07:26,390 --> 00:07:29,180
so carbon dioxide can diffuse in.

151
00:07:29,680 --> 00:07:31,790
So, from top to bottom:

152
00:07:31,790 --> 00:07:33,740
cuticle, upper epidermis,

153
00:07:33,740 --> 00:07:35,110
palisade mesophyll,

154
00:07:35,110 --> 00:07:37,600
spongy mesophyll, vascular bundle,

155
00:07:37,600 --> 00:07:41,080
lower epidermis with
stomata and guard cells.

156
00:07:44,430 --> 00:07:48,870
So how can you show that a leaf
has been photosynthesising?

157
00:07:48,870 --> 00:07:50,420
Test it for starch,

158
00:07:50,420 --> 00:07:54,520
because a leaf stores some
of its glucose as starch.

159
00:07:55,020 --> 00:07:57,370
First, destarch the plant.

160
00:07:57,370 --> 00:08:00,570
Put it in the dark for a day or two.

161
00:08:00,570 --> 00:08:03,490
With no light, it
can't photosynthesise,

162
00:08:03,490 --> 00:08:06,220
so it uses up its stored starch.

163
00:08:06,220 --> 00:08:10,840
That means any starch you find later
must have been made during your

164
00:08:10,840 --> 00:08:13,530
experiment. Step one:

165
00:08:13,530 --> 00:08:17,380
put the leaf in boiling
water for about a minute.

166
00:08:17,380 --> 00:08:19,030
This kills the cells,

167
00:08:19,030 --> 00:08:21,560
and breaks down the cell membranes,

168
00:08:21,560 --> 00:08:25,590
so the iodine can get
in later. Step two:

169
00:08:25,590 --> 00:08:27,890
turn off the Bunsen burner.

170
00:08:27,890 --> 00:08:31,380
Then put the leaf in a
boiling tube of ethanol,

171
00:08:31,380 --> 00:08:34,010
and stand it in the hot water.

172
00:08:34,010 --> 00:08:35,570
Ethanol is flammable,

173
00:08:35,570 --> 00:08:38,590
so never heat it with a naked flame.

174
00:08:38,590 --> 00:08:41,370
The hot ethanol removes
the chlorophyll,

175
00:08:41,370 --> 00:08:46,180
so the colour change will
be easy to see. Step three:

176
00:08:46,180 --> 00:08:48,570
dip the leaf in warm water.

177
00:08:48,570 --> 00:08:50,710
The ethanol makes it brittle,

178
00:08:50,710 --> 00:08:54,310
and the water softens it. Step four:

179
00:08:54,310 --> 00:08:56,780
spread the leaf on a white tile,

180
00:08:56,780 --> 00:08:59,100
so the colour is easy to see,

181
00:08:59,100 --> 00:09:01,260
and add iodine solution.

182
00:09:01,560 --> 00:09:03,260
If it turns blue-black,

183
00:09:03,260 --> 00:09:04,930
starch is present.

184
00:09:04,930 --> 00:09:06,730
If it stays orange-brown,

185
00:09:06,730 --> 00:09:08,450
there's no starch.

186
00:09:11,800 --> 00:09:16,290
Now you can use that test to
show what photosynthesis needs.

187
00:09:16,290 --> 00:09:18,840
Each experiment needs a control.

188
00:09:18,840 --> 00:09:21,460
A control is identical to the test,

189
00:09:21,460 --> 00:09:24,890
except for the one factor
you're investigating.

190
00:09:24,890 --> 00:09:28,940
It shows that the result
was caused by that factor.

191
00:09:29,440 --> 00:09:31,260
First, chlorophyll.

192
00:09:31,260 --> 00:09:34,560
Take a destarched plant
with variegated leaves:

193
00:09:34,560 --> 00:09:38,080
leaves that are partly
green and partly white.

194
00:09:38,080 --> 00:09:40,920
The white parts have no chlorophyll.

195
00:09:40,920 --> 00:09:43,870
Leave it in the light
for a few hours,

196
00:09:43,870 --> 00:09:45,580
then test a leaf.

197
00:09:45,580 --> 00:09:48,420
Only the green parts turn blue-black.

198
00:09:48,420 --> 00:09:51,020
The white parts stay orange-brown.

199
00:09:51,020 --> 00:09:53,660
The green parts are the control.

200
00:09:53,660 --> 00:09:55,870
So chlorophyll is needed.

201
00:09:56,370 --> 00:09:57,940
Second, light.

202
00:09:57,940 --> 00:09:59,740
Take a destarched plant,

203
00:09:59,740 --> 00:10:03,250
and cover part of one
leaf with black paper.

204
00:10:03,250 --> 00:10:06,460
Leave it in the light
for a few hours.

205
00:10:06,460 --> 00:10:10,760
After the test, only the
uncovered part turns blue-black.

206
00:10:10,760 --> 00:10:13,500
The uncovered part is the control.

207
00:10:13,500 --> 00:10:15,410
So light is needed.

208
00:10:15,910 --> 00:10:17,970
Third, carbon dioxide.

209
00:10:17,970 --> 00:10:19,770
Take a destarched plant,

210
00:10:19,770 --> 00:10:21,270
and seal one leaf,

211
00:10:21,270 --> 00:10:24,720
still attached, inside
a flask with soda lime,

212
00:10:24,720 --> 00:10:27,030
which absorbs carbon dioxide.

213
00:10:27,030 --> 00:10:29,510
The control is an identical flask,

214
00:10:29,510 --> 00:10:31,270
with no soda lime.

215
00:10:31,270 --> 00:10:33,690
After a few hours in the light,

216
00:10:33,690 --> 00:10:36,630
only the control leaf
turns blue-black.

217
00:10:36,630 --> 00:10:39,080
So carbon dioxide is needed.

218
00:10:42,430 --> 00:10:45,890
Next: how fast is
photosynthesis happening?

219
00:10:45,890 --> 00:10:47,410
That's its rate.

220
00:10:47,410 --> 00:10:51,160
To measure it, use
pondweed, a water plant.

221
00:10:51,160 --> 00:10:54,960
Put it in water with a little
sodium hydrogencarbonate,

222
00:10:54,960 --> 00:10:57,320
which supplies carbon dioxide.

223
00:10:57,320 --> 00:11:02,730
In the light, the pondweed gives
off bubbles of gas, mostly oxygen.

224
00:11:03,030 --> 00:11:05,430
Count the bubbles per minute.

225
00:11:05,430 --> 00:11:07,810
Or, for more accurate results,

226
00:11:07,810 --> 00:11:10,630
collect the gas and
measure its volume,

227
00:11:10,630 --> 00:11:13,720
because bubbles can
be different sizes.

228
00:11:14,220 --> 00:11:16,410
To change the light intensity,

229
00:11:16,410 --> 00:11:19,290
move a lamp closer or further away.

230
00:11:19,290 --> 00:11:20,890
The closer the lamp,

231
00:11:20,890 --> 00:11:23,390
the higher the light intensity.

232
00:11:23,390 --> 00:11:26,930
So, light intensity is
the independent variable:

233
00:11:26,930 --> 00:11:28,740
the one you change.

234
00:11:28,740 --> 00:11:31,350
The rate is the dependent variable:

235
00:11:31,350 --> 00:11:33,210
the one you measure.

236
00:11:33,210 --> 00:11:36,260
And everything else
must be kept constant:

237
00:11:36,260 --> 00:11:40,110
the same plant, the same
carbon dioxide concentration,

238
00:11:40,110 --> 00:11:41,670
the same temperature,

239
00:11:41,670 --> 00:11:43,770
and no other lights on.

240
00:11:43,770 --> 00:11:46,010
To keep the temperature steady,

241
00:11:46,010 --> 00:11:48,790
stand the beaker in a water bath.

242
00:11:48,790 --> 00:11:50,290
An LED lamp helps,

243
00:11:50,290 --> 00:11:54,730
because it gives off much less
heat than a filament bulb.

244
00:11:55,030 --> 00:11:56,680
At each new distance,

245
00:11:56,680 --> 00:11:59,350
wait a few minutes before you count,

246
00:11:59,350 --> 00:12:01,500
so the plant can adjust.

247
00:12:01,500 --> 00:12:04,530
Then repeat, and calculate a mean.

248
00:12:05,030 --> 00:12:08,830
You can test the other
two factors the same way.

249
00:12:08,830 --> 00:12:11,560
Just change one thing at a time.

250
00:12:11,560 --> 00:12:13,310
To vary carbon dioxide,

251
00:12:13,310 --> 00:12:17,200
use different concentrations
of sodium hydrogencarbonate.

252
00:12:17,200 --> 00:12:18,710
To vary temperature,

253
00:12:18,710 --> 00:12:22,190
set the water bath to
different temperatures.

254
00:12:23,340 --> 00:12:25,250
Here are the results.

255
00:12:25,250 --> 00:12:27,300
As light intensity increases,

256
00:12:27,300 --> 00:12:30,100
the rate of photosynthesis increases.

257
00:12:30,100 --> 00:12:32,010
Then it levels off.

258
00:12:32,310 --> 00:12:35,100
Increase the carbon
dioxide concentration,

259
00:12:35,100 --> 00:12:37,310
and you get the same shape:

260
00:12:37,310 --> 00:12:38,770
the rate increases,

261
00:12:38,770 --> 00:12:40,440
then levels off.

262
00:12:40,740 --> 00:12:42,760
Temperature is different.

263
00:12:42,760 --> 00:12:45,430
The rate increases up to an optimum,

264
00:12:45,430 --> 00:12:47,150
then falls quickly.

265
00:12:47,150 --> 00:12:52,100
That's because the reactions of
photosynthesis are catalysed by enzymes.

266
00:12:52,100 --> 00:12:53,510
Below the optimum,

267
00:12:53,510 --> 00:12:57,760
raising the temperature gives the
molecules more kinetic energy,

268
00:12:57,760 --> 00:13:02,450
so there are more frequent effective
collisions between enzymes and their

269
00:13:02,450 --> 00:13:05,000
substrates. Above the optimum,

270
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:07,160
the enzymes are denatured.

271
00:13:07,160 --> 00:13:09,450
Their active sites change shape,

272
00:13:09,450 --> 00:13:12,190
so the substrates no longer fit.

273
00:13:12,690 --> 00:13:15,460
When a question says
describe a graph,

274
00:13:15,460 --> 00:13:19,200
say what happens, and quote
numbers from the axes,

275
00:13:19,200 --> 00:13:20,820
with their units.

276
00:13:20,820 --> 00:13:23,650
When it says explain, say why.

277
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:29,190
Now let's explain those shapes,

278
00:13:29,190 --> 00:13:31,410
using limiting factors.

279
00:13:31,410 --> 00:13:36,320
A limiting factor is something in
short supply that limits the rate of a

280
00:13:36,320 --> 00:13:37,410
process.

281
00:13:37,910 --> 00:13:40,060
Back to the light graph.

282
00:13:40,060 --> 00:13:41,660
On this rising part,

283
00:13:41,660 --> 00:13:45,190
the rate increases as
light intensity increases.

284
00:13:45,190 --> 00:13:48,420
So light intensity is
the limiting factor.

285
00:13:48,420 --> 00:13:49,920
On this flat part,

286
00:13:49,920 --> 00:13:52,420
more light makes no difference.

287
00:13:52,420 --> 00:13:56,090
Light intensity is no
longer the limiting factor.

288
00:13:56,090 --> 00:13:57,500
Something else is,

289
00:13:57,500 --> 00:14:01,330
like carbon dioxide
concentration, or temperature.

290
00:14:01,830 --> 00:14:06,580
Now repeat the experiment at a
higher carbon dioxide concentration.

291
00:14:06,580 --> 00:14:08,330
At low light intensity,

292
00:14:08,330 --> 00:14:10,510
the two curves are the same,

293
00:14:10,510 --> 00:14:14,380
because light intensity is
still the limiting factor.

294
00:14:14,380 --> 00:14:17,440
But the new curve keeps
rising for longer,

295
00:14:17,440 --> 00:14:19,400
and levels off higher.

296
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:24,430
That shows carbon dioxide was the
limiting factor on the flat part.

297
00:14:24,930 --> 00:14:27,890
In the exam, name
the limiting factor,

298
00:14:27,890 --> 00:14:29,570
and give the reason:

299
00:14:29,570 --> 00:14:32,270
increasing it increases the rate.

300
00:14:32,770 --> 00:14:36,460
Different conditions have
different limiting factors.

301
00:14:36,460 --> 00:14:38,820
At dawn, or on a dull day,

302
00:14:38,820 --> 00:14:42,040
light intensity is usually
the limiting factor,

303
00:14:42,040 --> 00:14:44,490
because there's not much light.

304
00:14:44,490 --> 00:14:46,280
On a cold winter's day,

305
00:14:46,280 --> 00:14:48,150
it's often temperature.

306
00:14:48,150 --> 00:14:50,880
The molecules have
less kinetic energy,

307
00:14:50,880 --> 00:14:53,920
so there are fewer
effective collisions.

308
00:14:53,920 --> 00:14:56,680
And on a bright, warm summer's day,

309
00:14:56,680 --> 00:14:59,160
there's plenty of light and warmth,

310
00:14:59,160 --> 00:15:02,300
so it's often carbon
dioxide concentration.

311
00:15:02,300 --> 00:15:06,640
There's only a tiny amount of
carbon dioxide in the air.

312
00:15:09,990 --> 00:15:12,010
One more practical.

313
00:15:12,010 --> 00:15:16,210
Hydrogencarbonate indicator shows
how much carbon dioxide is in a

314
00:15:16,210 --> 00:15:21,630
solution. At the normal level of
carbon dioxide in air, it's red.

315
00:15:21,630 --> 00:15:23,480
With more carbon dioxide,

316
00:15:23,480 --> 00:15:25,050
it turns yellow.

317
00:15:25,050 --> 00:15:26,900
With less carbon dioxide,

318
00:15:26,900 --> 00:15:28,570
it turns purple.

319
00:15:29,070 --> 00:15:31,810
Here are three tubes of indicator.

320
00:15:31,810 --> 00:15:33,660
They're sealed with bungs,

321
00:15:33,660 --> 00:15:37,840
so no carbon dioxide from
the air can get in or out.

322
00:15:37,840 --> 00:15:40,770
One has pondweed, in bright light.

323
00:15:40,770 --> 00:15:42,420
One has pondweed too,

324
00:15:42,420 --> 00:15:44,890
but its tube is wrapped in foil,

325
00:15:44,890 --> 00:15:46,700
so it's dark inside.

326
00:15:46,700 --> 00:15:49,680
And one has no pondweed at all.

327
00:15:49,680 --> 00:15:51,960
What colour will each tube be,

328
00:15:51,960 --> 00:15:53,820
after a few hours?

329
00:15:54,320 --> 00:15:57,840
Pause the video, and
make your prediction.

330
00:16:02,190 --> 00:16:04,210
Here's what happens.

331
00:16:04,210 --> 00:16:07,580
In the light, the
indicator turns purple.

332
00:16:07,580 --> 00:16:10,370
Photosynthesis is faster
than respiration,

333
00:16:10,370 --> 00:16:15,200
so the pondweed takes in more
carbon dioxide than it gives out.

334
00:16:15,500 --> 00:16:18,180
In the dark, it turns yellow.

335
00:16:18,180 --> 00:16:19,940
There's no photosynthesis,

336
00:16:19,940 --> 00:16:21,890
but respiration carries on,

337
00:16:21,890 --> 00:16:25,170
so the pondweed gives
out carbon dioxide.

338
00:16:25,470 --> 00:16:28,400
The tube with no pondweed stays red.

339
00:16:28,400 --> 00:16:30,070
That's the control.

340
00:16:30,070 --> 00:16:34,130
It shows that the pondweed
caused the colour changes.

341
00:16:34,430 --> 00:16:38,270
And in dim light, the
two rates can be equal.

342
00:16:38,270 --> 00:16:42,160
Then there's no net uptake or
release of carbon dioxide,

343
00:16:42,160 --> 00:16:44,560
so the indicator stays red.

344
00:16:45,060 --> 00:16:47,180
Which busts a classic myth:

345
00:16:47,180 --> 00:16:49,920
that plants only respire at night.

346
00:16:49,920 --> 00:16:52,010
Plants respire all the time,

347
00:16:52,010 --> 00:16:54,690
day and night, just like you.

348
00:16:54,690 --> 00:16:58,100
In bright light,
photosynthesis is just faster,

349
00:16:58,100 --> 00:17:01,370
so there's a net uptake
of carbon dioxide.

350
00:17:01,370 --> 00:17:02,860
Net means overall:

351
00:17:02,860 --> 00:17:07,200
the plant takes in more carbon
dioxide than it gives out.

352
00:17:07,200 --> 00:17:10,180
Net is the word examiners look for.

353
00:17:11,330 --> 00:17:14,160
So, back to van Helmont's willow.

354
00:17:14,160 --> 00:17:17,790
Where did those seventy-four
kilograms come from?

355
00:17:18,190 --> 00:17:20,520
Carbon dioxide, from the air,

356
00:17:20,520 --> 00:17:22,910
and water, from the soil.

357
00:17:22,910 --> 00:17:24,420
Joined into glucose,

358
00:17:24,420 --> 00:17:26,220
using energy from light,

359
00:17:26,220 --> 00:17:28,120
then built into cellulose,

360
00:17:28,120 --> 00:17:29,990
starch and proteins.

361
00:17:30,290 --> 00:17:34,130
The little that the soil lost
was mostly mineral ions,

362
00:17:34,130 --> 00:17:36,440
like nitrate and magnesium.

363
00:17:36,840 --> 00:17:40,500
Van Helmont thought his
tree was made of water.

364
00:17:40,500 --> 00:17:42,700
He was only partly right.

365
00:17:42,700 --> 00:17:45,380
A living tree is full of water.

366
00:17:45,380 --> 00:17:49,510
But most of the wood itself
was built from carbon dioxide,

367
00:17:49,510 --> 00:17:51,660
taken out of thin air.

368
00:17:52,810 --> 00:17:54,340
Let's recap.

369
00:17:54,340 --> 00:17:59,060
Photosynthesis: carbon dioxide plus
water gives glucose plus oxygen,

370
00:17:59,060 --> 00:18:02,240
in the presence of
light and chlorophyll.

371
00:18:02,240 --> 00:18:06,800
Chlorophyll transfers energy from
light into energy in chemicals.

372
00:18:06,800 --> 00:18:09,090
Glucose is used for respiration,

373
00:18:09,090 --> 00:18:10,600
starch, cellulose,

374
00:18:10,600 --> 00:18:12,320
sucrose and nectar.

375
00:18:12,320 --> 00:18:15,740
Nitrate ions are needed
to make amino acids.

376
00:18:15,740 --> 00:18:19,170
Magnesium ions are needed
to make chlorophyll.

377
00:18:19,170 --> 00:18:21,110
Leaves are broad, thin,

378
00:18:21,110 --> 00:18:22,710
and built in layers,

379
00:18:22,710 --> 00:18:25,170
each adapted for photosynthesis.

380
00:18:25,170 --> 00:18:29,910
Light intensity, carbon dioxide
concentration and temperature can all be

381
00:18:29,910 --> 00:18:31,540
limiting factors.

382
00:18:32,040 --> 00:18:34,300
And that's plant nutrition.
